From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 05:45:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-12a driver-gap data planes

Add register-file data planes for the batch-12a driver-gap Units on the
reconciled canonical chain. The register tables come from the batch11
driver-gap protocol research (official protocol PDFs/MDs); no Unit driver is
present in the tree and no electrical/mechanical/optical behavior is modeled.

Base in the reconciled canonical order is the 37-layer chain through 0157
(canonical 75f1d24 plus 0120-0129, 0131, 0134, 0136, 0130, 0133, 0135, 0132,
0137, 0138, 0139, 0140, 0141, 0142, 0143, 0144, 0145, 0146, 0147, 0148, 0149,
0150, 0151, 0152, 0153 and 0154, plus the 0156 ATECC wake fix and the 0157
glass M5GFX protocol fix); this is the 38th layer after 0120 and it applies at
the chain end. Its control-kind registration, struct fields and supported-ids
entries were merged mechanically with the glass layer's additions.
- byteswitch (U191 0x46) / bytebutton (U192 0x47): one shared CONTROL_BYTEUNIT
  model. State bitmap 0x00 and per-channel 0x60-0x67 (0 = pressed/closed per the
  driver convention, physical polarity UNRESOLVED), LED brightness 0x10-0x18,
  LED mode 0x19, user RGB888 0x20-0x4F with the documented
  base=0x20+(n/4)*0x10+(n%4)*4 layout, system RGB 0x70-0xAF, save 0xF0, IRQ
  0xF1, firmware 0xFE and address 0xFF. QOM fixtures: state-bitmap, brightness,
  led-mode, rgb-hex, irq-enable/count, save-count, firmware-version.
- step16 (U198 0x48): position 0x00, LED config 0x10, brightness 0x20,
  direction 0x30, RGB power/brightness 0x40/0x41, RGB 0x50-0x52, save 0xF0,
  firmware/address. Fixtures: position, led-config, led-brightness, direction,
  rgb, rgb-power, rgb-brightness.
- timerpwr (U189 0x56): Grove output 0x00, backlight 0x01, button 0x10,
  wake/sleep trigger 0x20/0x21, schedule-on 0x30-0x32, sleep/cycle 0x40/0x41,
  USB/Grove V+I 0x60-0x6F (LE32 raw/100), battery V/I 0x70/0x74 (battery mV/10,
  current mA/100), schedule-off 0x80-0x82, charging 0x90, save/firmware/address.
- mq (U199 0x11): mode 0x00, LED 0x01, heat high/low 0x10/0x11, ADC8/ADC12
  0x20/0x30, valid 0x40 (the frozen-driver semantics get_valid_tags()==1 are
  used; the protocol PDF says 0 = valid - recorded as a blocker), NTC
  ADC/ohms 0x50/0x60/0x70 and reference/MQ/NTC mV 0x80-0x85. All values are
  synthetic fixture-derived conversions; gas/heater physics are NOT modeled.
- 8servos2-i2c (U222 0x25-0x34): channel modes 0x00, pull 0x10, input 0x20,
  output 0x30, ADC 0x40, servo 0x50, RGB config 0x60, PWM 0x70, RGB buffer
  0x80-0xBF, timer frequencies 0xD0, UID 0xE0, system telemetry 0xF0,
  firmware/address. The rotary fixture maps the I2C address over 0x25-0x34.
- cardkb2 (U215 0x5F): legacy I2C subset only (raw key byte at 0x00 and
  firmware version via pointer 0xF1). The UART AA03 frame mode, v2 report,
  BLE HID and ESP-NOW are separate attachment kinds and are NOT modeled.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 board, no guest) covers all seven attachments: property
registration, fixture read/write, range/time rejection and the rotary address
mapping. It is not a functional PASS and no Unit is promoted to implemented.
